  "investment-fee": {
    "heading": "Distinguish charged fees from the loss of future growth",
    "intro": "Use $10,000 initially, $1,000 deposited at each year end and twenty years. The first two rows enter an 8% return before fund fees; the next two use an equivalent 7.784% return already after the 0.20% fund fee. These annual contributions differ from the Mutual Fund calculator’s monthly deposit examples.",
    "columns": [
      "Scenario",
      "Entered return basis",
      "A ending balance",
      "A model-charged fees",
      "A reduction from further deductions",
      "B ending balance"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Returns apply to opening assets, then the applicable fund fee and a separate advisor fee are charged; the annual deposit arrives afterward. The total fee amount and the ending-balance reduction are different because paid fees also stop earning future growth.",
      "An 8% pre-fee return with a 0.20% fund charge gives (1.08 × 0.998 − 1) × 100 = 7.784% after that fund charge. The two return-basis pairs therefore end at the same balances before display rounding when all other assumptions match.",
      "For After fund fees, the fund charge is not deducted again. Model-charged fees exclude fund costs already embedded in the return. Zero further deductions or a zero balance reduction on that row does not mean the investment has no expense ratio or no economic cost.",
      "The comparison row keeps one 8% pre-fee return and the same deposits for A and B, changing only the fund fee from 0.20% to 0.05%. Identical net-return inputs would already include each fund’s costs and cannot isolate a gross-fee advantage.",
      "This annual model excludes sales loads, taxes, trading costs and tiered advisor contracts. Use Mutual Fund for its monthly/annual contributions and entry/exit charge assumptions. Do not rank the two tools’ balances without matching their cash-flow and charging conventions."
    ],
    "guidePath": "/guides/mutual-fund-fees-and-investment-costs/",
    "related": [
      {
        "href": "/mutual-fund-calculator",
        "label": "Project entry loads, annual expenses and a final exit charge"
      }
    ],
