  "cd": {
    "heading": "Compare CD terms without mixing APY and nominal rate",
    "intro": "These examples use one $10,000 deposit and an assumed constant 4% quote. Match both the term and the rate type. Longer terms earn for longer in this illustration; actual CD offers can have different yields by term.",
    "columns": [
      "Scenario",
      "Rate convention",
      "Term",
      "Interest earned",
      "Before-tax maturity",
      "After modeled tax"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "For APY, maturity = initial deposit × (1 + APY)^(months / 12). A 14-month term is entered as zero years plus fourteen months; twelve months is not fourteen, and a bank’s exact day-count convention can differ.",
      "The compounding selector is ignored for an APY quote because APY already includes compounding. A nominal 4% rate compounded monthly instead uses (1 + 0.04/12)^months and therefore differs from 4% APY.",
      "The 22% tax row applies an entered haircut to positive total interest at maturity. It is not a determination of actual tax liability, annual tax timing or account eligibility. Before-tax interest and after-tax proceeds remain separate.",
      "The monthly schedule shows accrued interest with earnings left invested, not an automatic monthly cash payout. The model does not support monthly withdrawals or additional monthly deposits on this CD; use Savings for recurring deposits.",
      "No live bank rates, early-withdrawal penalty, changing rate, renewal or deposit-insurance eligibility is inferred. Consult account terms; use the separate early-withdrawal calculator for a penalty scenario."
    ],
    "guidePath": "/guides/apr-vs-apy/",
    "related": [
